\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Campaign activity rasters: every ledgered LLM attempt (kills, errors, OK calls) and every scored proposal (colored by score) across generations and chunks, for the V5, V6, and V7 (first three chunks) campaigns. Scored-proposal density rises era over era (37 $\rightarrow $ 140 $\rightarrow $ 160$^{+}$) even as the oracle hardens, because repair loops, compounding cross-run memory, and the strict-schema transport convert more of the model ensemble's output into adjudicable physics.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
